  "term": "lysergic acid diethylamide",
  "definition": "Lysergic acid diethylamide is a semisynthetic substance derived from ergot that has complex effects on serotonin systems in the body and brain. It is a powerful hallucinogen, although its hallucinogenic action is not fully understood.",
